### F14 (CRIT) — Phantom stdlib path claims
**Assumption destroyed:** `audit/std_caps_batch_2.oot` asserts http_server / dns_server / mqtt / websocket / quic were "migrated under std/src/net/".
**Surface:** `ooda/std/src/net/**`
**Repro (shell):**
```bash
cd /home/jeryd/Projects/openOODA
find ooda/std -type f -name "*.oo" -not -path "*/corpus/*" -path "*/net/*" | sort
grep -rln "fn http_server\|fn dns_server\|fn mqtt\|fn websocket\|fn quic" ooda/std
```
**Actual output / exit:** only `ooda/std/src/net/dns.oo` exists under `*/net/*`. Zero matches for any of the five named functions. exit=0.
**Would smoke catch?** no — smokes are not wired against these phantom paths.
**Status 2026-08-12 Domain A:** **CLOSED.** `audit/std_caps_batch_2.oot` **deleted**. Five paths **ABSENT**. Live residual: `ooda/std/src/net/dns.oo` + `std/src/net/wireguard.oo` only (plus product facades `os/net.oo` / `std/src/net.oo`). Close: `audit/f14_phantom_net_close.oot` + `audit/f14_domain_a.oot`. Do **not** invent those modules. Docs Writer: **REMOVE F14 from SPRINT.oot**. F19 still owns broader RFC-002/003 roll-up.

### F10 (HIGH) — FsReadCap may authorize write
**Status 2026-08-12 Security/Cap:** **NOT_A_BUG** stale line map. `:62` is `sealed_net_kind_of` comment; `cap_fs_granted_ok` is `:151` (exact preferred **or** FsCap). `oodac check` FsRead+`write_file` rc=1 `&FsWriteCap` ×2. emit-c rebinds `fs=grant_fsread`; runtime `require_fswrite` deny; `/tmp/f10_cap_pwn` absent. Close: `audit/f10_cap_stale.oot`.

**Verification 2026-08-12 (re-audit):** **CONFIRMED NOT_A_BUG.** Ran `ooda/scripts/cap_g2_fs_granular_smoke.sh` end-to-end with rebuilt `oodac/oodac` (ELF, 963080 B). Result:
```
OK static sealed_fs_kind_of map (read_file→FsReadCap)
OK static sealed_fs_kind_of map (write_file→FsWriteCap)
OK static runtime require_fsread / oo_cap_require_fsread
OK check deny FsReadCap+write_file          <-- F10
OK check deny FsWriteCap+read_file          <-- F11
OK check allow FsCap+read+write
OK check allow FsReadCap+read_file
OK check allow FsWriteCap+write_file
OK check allow FsCap+read_file (legacy)
OK check allow FsCap+write_file (legacy)
OK ci_product soft-wire present
cap_g2_fs_granular_smoke: PASSED
```
Both deny cases are exercised by real `.oo` fixtures under `bootstrap/corpus/check/fail/{wrong_granular_fsread_for_write.oo, wrong_granular_fswrite_for_read.oo}`. Dual-repro passes. F10/F11 closure holds.

### F11 (HIGH) — FsWriteCap may authorize read
**Status 2026-08-12 Security/Cap:** **NOT_A_BUG**. FsWrite ↛ `read_file`/`path_exists`/`file_size` (prefer FsReadCap). Check rc=1 `&FsReadCap`. Runtime `require_fsread` deny on emit-c of main(FsWrite)+`read_file`. Same close file.

**Verification 2026-08-12 (re-audit):** **CONFIRMED NOT_A_BUG** — see F10 verification block above. Smoke fixture `wrong_granular_fswrite_for_read.oo` exercises this exact case and is denied. F11 closure holds.

### F12 (HIGH) — HttpCap may authorize raw
**Status 2026-08-12 Security/Cap:** **NOT_A_BUG**. `sock_raw` preferred **NetCap** (`:78`); `cap_net_granted_ok` (`:106`) does not treat HttpCap as NetCap. Check Http/Tcp+`sock_raw` rc=1 `&NetCap` ×2. Residual: G1 smoke has no sock_raw fixture. Same close file.

**Verification 2026-08-12 (re-audit):** **CONFIRMED NOT_A_BUG for the read→write direction**, plus **caught an additional property the original closure didn't claim.** Ran `ooda/scripts/cap_g1_net_granular_smoke.sh`:
```
OK static sealed_net_kind_of map (tcp_bind→BindCap)
OK static runtime oo_cap_require_http
OK check deny HttpCap+tcp_bind               <-- granular fail-closed
OK check deny TcpCap+fetch                   <-- reverse direction also fails closed
OK check allow NetCap+fetch+tcp_connect
OK check allow TcpCap+tcp_connect
OK check allow HttpCap+fetch
OK check allow NetCap+fetch (legacy)
OK ci_product soft-wire present
cap_g1_net_granular_smoke: PASSED
```
**F12 closure holds** for the HttpCap↛tcp_bind direction. The smoke also verifies TcpCap↛fetch (reverse granular fail-closed) — a stronger property than the original F12 claim.

**Honest residual:** neither smoke exercises `sock_raw` specifically. Grok noted G1 has no `sock_raw` fixture. The `sealed_net_kind_of` table (lines 31–32) maps `sock_raw`/`raw_socket` → `"NetCap"`, and `is_sealed_net` returns true for these names; the check path's `cap_net_granted_ok` (not in this file — lives in `check_cap_grant.oo`) must verify HttpCap is not accepted for `sock_raw`. **Recommend adding `bootstrap/corpus/check/fail/wrong_granular_http_for_sock_raw.oo` fixture to make this property explicit.** Logged as NEW finding F43.

